    {
     "url": "http://calcashmere.com/svc-dehair.htm",
     "page_type": "other_official",
     "text": "Cashmere Dehairing, Speaking, Classes, Tours. Scouring & Custom Dehairing. The first step in processing is a gentle yet thorough washing. Dehairing is the process of separating undesirable matter, including guard hair from the cashmere fiber. Separating hair from cashmere efficiently is a unique multifaceted process that requires specialized equipment and modern technology. After dehairing, the purified cashmere fiber (known in the industry as sliver or web) is ready for the spinning wheel to undergo a metamorphosis into fine cashmere yarn; then to the knitter for creating one of a kind luxurious knitwear apparels. What Makes us Unique: State-of-the-art technology to process any lot size. Lot size and content according to your preference. Dehairing system designed for sheared or combed cashmere fiber. Each order is pampered. Eeach order and lot processed separately preventing cross contamination. Experienced in the business of cashmere. Specialized equipment calibrated to process qualifying cashmere fiber. Processing Fees. Estimating Processing Fees: Fees are calculated on individual lots within an order. Scouring charges are based on lot received weight. Dehairing charges are based on yield (the percentage difference in lot received weight and lot finished weight.). Processing Fee Schedule & Authorization (PDF file). Please contact California Cashmere Company to discuss fees and schedules for orders greater than 500 pounds. Billing Procedures: Scouring requires pre-payment of the entire scouring fee. Dehairing requires a deposit of at least 1/2 estimated cost of processing, in addition to scouring fee. Orders will be invoiced when completed. Upon receipt of payment orders will be shipped. For immediate shipment of completed orders, payment by VISA/MasterCard/Discover/AMEX are accepted. PRODUCT • SERVICE • INFORMATION • AL-RAFIQ FARM • CASHMERE FIBER ASSOCIATION • HOME. Page 1 • 2 • 3 • 4 • 5.",
