     "page_type": "manufacturing",
     "text": "dehairing facility. Our in-house dehairing facilities ensure precise separation of fine cashmere fibers from coarse guard hairs, preserving fiber length and softness at the source. Baina Cashmere has been engaged in the cashmere business since 1986, initially supplying fiber to world-renowned yarn manufacturers such as Todd & Duncan in Scotland and Carriage in Italy. By owning and operating our own facilities, Baina Cashmere is able to transform high-quality raw materials into high-purity, premium cashmere fiber, ensuring an ideal foundation for downstream production. With years of industry experience and advanced dehairing equipment, our process is both precise and efficient — effectively removing impurities and coarse fibers to produce cashmere that is soft, fine, pure, and highly durable. We remain committed to environmentally responsible and sustainable practices, continuously refining our processes to provide high-quality raw materials and tailored solutions to our partners. Baina Cashmere operates two specialized facilities dedicated to the dehairing of raw cashmere — Shufu Dehairing Factory in Hebei, and Erlianhot Dehairing Factory in Inner Mongolia. In 2004, we established our first modern dehairing facility, featuring one dehairing workshop, 45 skilled employees, 70 Qingdao Model 186 carding machines, and one Model 272 opening machine—delivering consistently high-quality raw materials to markets worldwide. As our business continued to expand, we opened a second dehairing facility in Erlianhot, Inner Mongolia in 2025. This new factory includes one dehairing workshop, 36 employees, 40 Qingdao Model 186 carding machines, and two Model 272 opening machines, enabling us to better serve the global demand for premium cashmere fiber. Address. No. 5 Wenchang South Road, International Cashmere Industrial Park, Qinghe County, Xingtai City, Hebei Province, China. Room 207, Weimu Warehousing & Logistics Office Building, North of Erman Line, West of Eurasia