    {
     "url": "https://www.zianhitech.com/",
     "page_type": "homepage",
     "text": "Zian Hi-Tech & Yunshang Cashmere. Skip to content. Contact us. Zian Hi-Tech · Yunshang Cashmere. The leading supply chain for sustainability-certified, high-quality cashmere fibre. For over 20 years, Zian Hi-Tech and Yunshang Cashmere have been recognised as a leading supply chain for the highest quality dehaired Chinese cashmere fibre and combed cashmere top, serving many illustrious European spinning and weaving mills. Our unique advantage comes from vertical control of the entire cashmere production chain and our firmly set principles, which allow sustainability improvements to be adopted rapidly. Today, we hold an outstanding reputation for the consistent quality of our fibre, our expertise in sustainable cashmere production practices, and the transparency of our service. Talk to us. Our certifications. Supplying the world's leading mills and brands since 1998. Founded. since 1998. Finest fibre. down to 14.5 µm. Combed top length. up to 50 mm. Coarse hair content. as low as <0.005 %. Who we are. Two companies, one cashmere supply chain. Zian Hi-Tech and Yunshang Cashmere work together so that the same team is accountable for your fibre from the herd to delivery. UK & Europe commercial arm · Since 1998. Zian Hi-Tech (U.K.) Limited. Our commercial arm for the UK and Europe, working directly with brands and European spinning and weaving mills on sales, partnerships, sustainability and service. Chinese production arm · Since 2009. Yunshang Cashmere (Xi'an) Co., Ltd. Our production company in Xi'an, sourcing raw cashmere from Inner Mongolia and processing it in our own dehairing plant into dehaired fibre and cashmere top. World's first Regenerative Organic Certified® cashmere supplier. Yunshang Cashmere. Founded in 2009, Yunshang Cashmere has earned a strong reputation in the high-end fashion and textile industry as a trusted supplier of premium cashmere fibre. Our success is built on consistency, reliability and innovation. By building close relationships with every stakeholder in the supply chain, from farmers to designers, we turn our customers' goals into tangible results. This integrated approach has made Yunshang one of the first certified organic cashmere suppliers in the industry and, more recently, the world's first Regenerative Organic Certified® cashmere supplier. Where our cashmere comes from. The grasslands of Inner Mongolia. Each spring, Yunshang sources raw cashmere from independent goat farmers in two regions of Inner Mongolia: Alashan and Erdos. The raw fibre then travels to our own dehairing plant in Xi'an. Every herd is assigned a unique ID, so each bale stays traceable to the farm it came from. Simplified map; boundaries approximate. Our sustainability. Sustainability is our leading principle. We are keen to share the actions that drive us towards it. 01. Animal welfare. We enforce an animal welfare code that our farmer suppliers must follow, so goats are bred, raised and combed in a cruelty-free way. We also work with local government and Chinese NGOs to protect goat herds and herdsmen during extreme weather. 02. Preserving the environment. Our farmers' goat herds graze freely across between 2.7 and 6.7 km² of grassland each. 03. Staff wellbeing. Yunshang is a Fair Wage certified employer. Every staff member is offered a full pension, free accommodation for themselves and their families, three free meals a day, free utilities, and a garden and outdoor exercise area. 04. Full traceability. Each cashmere herd is assigned a unique ID, and traceability is recorded throughout production, so we can always identify the individual farm our material comes from. Our certification journey. Each step independently audited, and often a first for the cashmere industry. 2020. SFA. Certified to the Sustainable Fibre Alliance Cashmere Standard. 2022. GOTS. Certified to the Global Organic Textile Standard. 2023. Fair for Life. Certified for fair trade and responsible supply chains. 2024. Regenerative Organic Certified®. Certified for soil health, animal welfare and social fairness. 2025. Textile Exchange LCA. Helped collect primary data for the first comprehensive life cycle assessment of cashmere. 2026. Fair Wage & emissions data. Fair Wage certified, and collecting emissions data across our farm and factory supply chain. We supply cashmere certified to SFA, GOTS, Fair for Life and Regenerative Organic standards, depending on origin and grade, and Yunshang is a Fair Wage certified employer. Verify each one on the certifier's own register: Sustainable Fibre Alliance. Animal welfare, rangeland health and responsible processing. sustainablefibre.org. Global Organic Textile Standard. Organic and ecological textiles, certified through Ecocert. View certificate. Fair for Life. Fair trade and responsible supply chains. View certificate. Regenerative Organic Certified®. Certified by the Regenerative Organic Alliance. View certificate. Fair Wage Certified. Fair Wage Network, valid 15 March 2026 to 15 March 2027. View certificate (PDF). Our product. Dehaired cashmere fibre and cashmere top. Only the highest quality, sustainable cashmere, sourced from Alashan and Erdos in Inner Mongolia. Fibre diameter. Down to 14.5 µm — we supply and process fibre as fine as 14.5 microns. Fibre length. Up to 44 mm dehaired · 50 mm combed top — dehaired fibre up to 44 millimetres and combed cashmere top up to 50 millimetres long. Coarse hair content. As low as <0.005% — exceptionally clean dehairing for a softer, purer fibre. Colour quality. White for white — no black or dark fibres and a maximum of 6 fawn fibres per 5 grams of cashmere, with whiteness above 70%. What is dehairing? Raw cashmere arrives mixed with the goat's coarse outer guard hair, grease and other contaminants. Dehairing removes them, leaving only the fine, soft undercoat that is spun into yarn and woven into fabric. For cashmere top, we then comb the dehaired fibre to a uniform length and fineness, ready for spinning mills to make worsted yarn, or for weavers to make worsted fabric. Our production. A vertically integrated supply chain, built over two decades. From raw fibre to delivery, every stage happens at our own plant in Xi'an. Raw fibre sorting First sort. Washing & scouring Removing grease and dirt. Clean fibre sorting Second sort & contaminant removal. Dehairing & carding Separating the fine undercoat. Combing Cashmere top only. Packaging & delivery Tested before shipping. Tested three ways. We take random samples at every stage of production and test them in our in-house lab for fineness, length, colour and contamination. Results are compared with like-for-like tests at our customers' own labs and at independent third-party laboratories, and we ship only once every party's requirements are met. Our site in Xi'an. Our 39,960 m² site brings production together with staff dormitories, a canteen and a garden for our team. Commercial and production, together. Zian Hi-Tech in the UK and Europe and Yunshang Cashmere in Xi'an work as one team, so quality, traceability and service are managed end to end. Our team. Talk to the people behind the fibre. Tom Thomson. Sales Manager. Over 45 years of experience in the cashmere and textile industries. tom@zianhitech.com. Kingma Ma. Business Development & Sustainability Manager. Focused on business development, partnerships and sustainability. kingma@zianhitech.com. Walter Fangi. Biella Sales Agent. Leads business development in Biella, Italy. info@commerciolaniero.it. Contact us. Are you a brand or mill interested in certified sustainable cashmere? Tell us what you're looking for and the right person will get back to you. Sales tom@zianhitech.com. Partnerships & sustainability kingma@zianhitech.com. Biella, Italy info@commerciolaniero.it. LinkedIn linkedin.com/company/zianhitech.",
     "retrieved_at": "2026-11-22T09:11:02+00:00"
